MHDevBlue said:
3: Is there a way I can turn down the master volume of a whole project? I've decided that the music ingame is a bit too loud, and it would be a pain to go through and turn down every individual song. I know it's not a disaster if I have to do that, but I'm wondering if there's a way to do it this way.
Click to expand...
Yes! I did exactly that for my own project. Save the following code as a .js file and load it as a plugin:
Spoiler
JavaScript:
(function() {
	// CONFIGURATION: Edit these values as you see fit
	// Master volume, as a fraction of the default level.
	const masterVolumeScale = 0.25; 
	// In settings, adjust volume by this increment (a percentage)
	const volumeIncrement = 20;
	// Maximum volume level to allow in settings
	const volumeMax = 100;

	// END CONFIGURATION: Don't touch anything below here
	WebAudio.setMasterVolume(masterVolumeScale);
	Window_Options.prototype.volumeOffset = function() {
		return volumeIncrement;
	};
	Window_Options.prototype.volumeMax = function() {
		return volumeMax;
	};
	Window_Options.prototype.adjustVolume = function(mode) {
		var symbol = this.commandSymbol(this.index());
		if(!this.isVolumeSymbol(symbol)) return false;
		var value = this.getConfigValue(symbol);
		switch(mode) {
			case -1: value -= this.volumeOffset(); break;
			case 1: value += this.volumeOffset(); break;
			case 0:
				value += this.volumeOffset();
				if(value > this.volumeMax()) {
					value = 0;
				}
				break;
		}
        value = value.clamp(0, this.volumeMax());
        this.changeValue(symbol, value);
		return true;
	};
	const old_optOk = Window_Options.prototype.processOk;
	Window_Options.prototype.processOk = function() {
		if(!this.adjustVolume(0)) old_optOk.call(this);
	};
	const old_optLeft = Window_Options.prototype.cursorLeft;
	Window_Options.prototype.cursorLeft = function() {
		if(!this.adjustVolume(-1)) old_optLeft.call(this);
	};
	const old_optRight = Window_Options.prototype.cursorRight;
	Window_Options.prototype.cursorRight = function() {
		if(!this.adjustVolume(1)) old_optRight.call(this);
	};
	ConfigManager.readVolume = function(config, name) {
		var value = config[name];
		if (value !== undefined) {
			return Number(value).clamp(0, volumeMax);
		} else {
			return 100;
		}
	};
})();
It was tested in MV, but I'm pretty sure it'll also work in MZ.
MHDevBlue said:
4: Is there a way to put a balloon over the top of a character who has a sidequest, that moves with them and goes away when it's finished?
Click to expand...
Yes! In your character's move route (either set their movement type to Custom, or use Set Movement Route), add two script calls with the following lines of code:
JavaScript:
$gameTemp.requestBalloon(this, 3)
if(this.isBalloonPlaying()) this._moveRouteIndex--
Replace 3 with the number of the balloon you want.
With a bit of tweaking, this approach could probably create a balloon that just sticks and doesn't bob around, but I'm not 100% what you'd need to change for that. It'll also get a bit more complicated if the character moves around (rather than standing in one place); you might not need the second line of code in that case.
If you want something more complicated, such as a balloon with text in it, you'll need a plugin. However, if the standard balloon icon system works but you just don't like the specific balloons (maybe you want a scroll icon for example), you can add extra balloons at the bottom of the Balloon.png file in img/system (or even edit the default ones). Make sure they conform to the grid if you do this.

